    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42570" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sapīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sapp-</span></b> ), i, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a kind of fir-</i> or
				<i>pine-tree</i>, Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				39, 75, § 193</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 6, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 12, 23, § 61</span></i>;
			cf. <i><span class="en">id.
				15, 10, 9, § 36</span></i> (al. sappium).—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the lower</i>, <i>smooth part of the fir-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1, 2,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 2,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 39, 76, §
		196</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
